{"t_ms": 15109859, "conversation_id": "conv_fixed_early_proxy_s3_055", "turn_id": 1, "actor": "system", "event_type": "retrieval_result", "payload": {"passages": ["Noise & Quiet Hours Policy\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nTo ensure a peaceful stay for all guests, quiet hours are observed daily from 10:00 PM to 7:00 AM. Guests are requested to keep television volumes low and avoid loud conversations or gatherings during this period. Repeated disturbances may result in warnings or further action by hotel management.", "# corpus/ \u2014 Hotel Documents\n\n**Owner: Lakshya**\n\n## What this folder is\n\nThe hotel's documents live here: the knowledge the assistant answers from. About 60 short \ndocuments covering things like pool and gym hours, check-in and check-out rules, menus, and \npolicies.\n\n## How to fill it\n\nSee the full instructions in `retrieval/README.md` (Step 1). In short:\n- Write ~60 short documents, one topic per file, as `.txt` or `.md`.\n- Make them realistic and varied.\n- Deliberately plant a few contradictions (e.g. one doc says the pool closes at 10 PM, \n  another says 9 PM) and keep a note of which ones, for a later experiment.\n\nThe index-building script reads every file in this folder, so anything you put here becomes \npart of the searchable knowledge.\n", "Pet Policy\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nThe hotel welcomes small domestic pets weighing up to 20 kg. A one-time cleaning fee of \u20b91500 applies per stay. Pets must remain on a leash in public areas and should not be left unattended inside guest rooms. Owners are fully responsible for any damage or disturbance caused by their pets."], "scores": [0.7219775915145874, 0.876779317855835, 0.9338210821151733], "filenames": ["55_noise_policy.txt", "README.md", "53_pet_policy_allowed.txt"], "timing_policy": "fixed_early_proxy", "timing_trigger": "fixed_early_proxy", "user_end_known_at_finish": true, "launch_offset_ms_vs_user_end": 0, "overlap_with_speech_ms": 0, "forecast_invalidated": false}}
